Package: @PACKAGE_ID@
Name: uutils coreutils
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCHITECTURE@
Description: The core command-line tools, rewritten in Rust
 ls, cp, mv, cat, sort, dd, du and around a hundred more, replacing the GNU
 versions in usr/bin with faster, clearer ones that speak the same options.
 Install this one by hand, with `dpkg -i --force-conflicts` -- installing it
 through Sileo or apt takes `rm` away in the middle of the job and leaves the
 device unable to finish. The originals are kept in
 usr/libexec/uutils/gnu-backup. stdbuf, chroot, chcon and runcon are left out
 because they cannot work on iOS.
Maintainer: OwnGoal Studio <not-gonna-reply@owngoal.dev>
Author: uutils developers <https://github.com/uutils/coreutils>
Section: Utilities
Priority: standard
Depends: firmware (>= @MIN_IOS@)
Provides: md5sum, sha1sum, dirname, kill, mktemp
Replaces: coreutils, system-cmds, shell-cmds (<< 207.40.1), text-cmds (<< 1:0), file-cmds (<< 272.250.1-1)
Conflicts: coreutils, shell-cmds (<< 207.40.1), text-cmds (<< 1:0), file-cmds (<< 272.250.1-1), system-cmds (<< 854.40.2-3)
